feat(qlora): compute LoRA delta in activation dtype for BF16 safety
scale: ~48 lines across 1 files [S]

- Introduce `linear_no_bias_t` helper function to apply `x @ w^T` projection, replicating `candle_nn::Linear`'s rank-3 input handling.
- Modify `QuantizedLinear::forward` to compute the LoRA delta (`x @ A^T @ B^T`) using the activation's dtype (BF16) instead of the LoRA parameters' dtype (F32). This avoids dtype mismatch panics when activations are BF16.
- Ensure LoRA A/B matrices are cast to the activation dtype for matmul operations, preserving trainable parameters in F32 while allowing BF16 activations.

